  "youtube": {
    "title": "Nervous? Talk To Yourself Like This #shorts",
    "description": "\"Why am I so nervous?\" makes it worse. \"Maya, you've prepared for this\" makes it better.\n\nIn experiments before a stressful speech, people who talked to themselves using their own name (or \"you\") instead of \"I\" gave better speeches, as judged by others, and dwelled on it less afterwards. Psychologists call it distanced self-talk: it lets you coach yourself like you'd coach a friend.\n\nBefore your next big moment, try one sentence to yourself, by name.\n\nResearch: Kross et al. (2014), \"Self-Talk as a Regulatory Mechanism\", Journal of Personality and Social Psychology.\n\n#shorts #anxiety #confidence #psychology #publicspeaking #animation #selfimprovement",
